@baseUrl = http://localhost:8787
@apiKey = tw_live_replace_with_a_test_key
@model = replace-with-an-enabled-model
@requestId = replace-with-a-request-uuid

### Health (liveness only; does not check the database or GrsAI)
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Read the enabled catalogue
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/models

### Non-streaming chat (requires a verified, enabled text model and funded account)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sample-chat-request-0001

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Reply with one short sentence." }
  ],
  "max_tokens": 64
}

### Create a media job (input fields must match that model's verified schema)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/generations
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sample-media-request-0001

{
  "model": "replace-with-an-enabled-image-model",
  "input": {
    "prompt": "A small red paper kite against a clear blue sky"
  }
}

### Poll a job or inspect a chat request
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/requests/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Retrieve a completed result before its expiry
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/requests/{{requestId}}/result
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Download media file 0 from a completed media result
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/files/{{requestId}}/0
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Check credits and latest usage
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/credits
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Purchase and API-key-management routes require a Supabase user access token.
### Never put a real key or token in this tracked example file.
